  "constraints_and_limits": {
    "bed_eye": "Use the user-established lying-patient camera: an eye/head region over the head end of the mattress, viewing toward the far board/TV and rotating left toward the window. The sources support near-mattress foreground perspective; they do not expose the pillow/head-end boundary or measure eye height, pitch, roll, or exact head translation. Do not claim that any independently adjusted generic room camera is a validated patient camera merely because a board silhouette fits.",
    "depth": "There is no supplied calibrated translation baseline, fixed focal metadata, exposed column cross-section, or known metric landmark. Nearby A/B and F differ mainly in viewing direction; G/H likewise may be predominantly head-look changes. Pure rotation cannot triangulate depth. The images constrain line incidence, screen silhouettes, ordering, and candidate projection consistency, not a unique metric column depth, rail offset, or room size. Even a joint fit retains global scale ambiguity without one real measurement.",
    "bounded_candidates": "Keep a family of source-consistent column/rail-depth candidates and report sensitivity. Strong constraints are black jamb locations, drape outer silhouettes, rail line directions, and visible bed/TV contours. The concealed pillar edge and track contact should be bounded priors rather than measured points.",
    "recommended_missing_view": "Most informative is a native oblique view from a genuinely laterally displaced and slightly raised eye position, with unchanged/known FOV and preferably a measured baseline. It should show the beige member on both sides of the gathered curtain, the actual track endpoint/contact, a black window jamb, and a mattress/head-end or bed-rail corner simultaneously. A further pan from the same eye point will not resolve hidden depth. If only one patient-position shot is possible, tilt down enough to include pillow/head end and both mattress side edges while retaining the pillar; this chiefly resolves the bed-eye relationship, not hidden column depth."
  },
  "mandatory_exclusions": [
    "Exclude all beige_to_curtain_transition and beige_light_ochre_transition_example features from physical-corner fitting.",
    "Do not treat a pale_gray_region_left boundary as a named wall/pillar/mullion vertex without further physical evidence.",
    "No pseudo-correspondence from same polyline index, same sampled row, or top image clipping.",
    "Do not use person/HUD silhouettes, exterior skyline points, or hidden edge continuation as fixed room geometry.",
    "Curved bed-board contour samples are silhouette guardrails, not mesh vertex correspondences."
  ]
